nodecode-checkup is a rewrite of iap's iap/hermes-guide:

  https://github.com/iap/hermes-guide
  commit 9690c41665c2de09043fa12f19c7c081247ab831

MIT, Copyright (c) 2019-present, Iko <6572003+iap@users.noreply.github.com> (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's idea — a read-only self-check that complements the
harness's own doctor instead of replacing it, finding per surface, each
finding carrying the reason and the fix — as a Nodecode cell with three
checks over this organism's own state: a declared config section that is
still half filled and the member it wants, a cell folder that loaded and
refused to start or a link whose folder is gone, and the standing notices
the organism's parts are raising right now. The plugin's command, its
in-session skill and its terminal command became `/checkup`, the `run_checkup`
tool and `(checkup:scan)`.

Left out: the plugin's skills tap (31 Hermes troubleshooting playbooks plus
an install and a configuration guide) and the scopes that read Hermes's own
layout — versions, MCP, hooks, memories, storage, sessions, update and the
`git ls-remote` release notice. Nodecode's `/doctor` already reads its
equivalents (model pin, store, disk, build, sections, keys, a release
waiting), and a playbook written against Hermes's paths would describe the
wrong program. Also left out: the plugin's opt-in `proactive` drift check at
session start and end; the checkup runs when asked.
